# InputPlumber — the input daemon: reads each board's pad/MCU (devices.d + capability maps) and
# presents one virtual X-Box Elite pad to OpenGamepadUI and every emulator. Built FROM SOURCE via
# the local PKGBUILD since 0.82.0 (a prebuilt.pin on the release tarball before that — see git
# history for the pin and its device-adoption notes); from source because of the patches:
#
#   0001  upstream PR #757 (shadowapex/input-layers-v2, 2026-10-19, based on v0.82.0 exactly):
#         input layers in device profiles. A mapping may target `layer: {name: x}`; while the
#         activating input is held (or latched with mode: toggle) the layer's mappings override
#         the base ones, releases are emitted for whatever the layer produced (no stuck keys),
#         and layers stack. This is the Guide-modifier mechanism for emulator hotkeys
#         (Guide+L1/R1/R2/Start), asked of ShadowApex 2026-10-18, answered with this PR.
#         Drop when a release carries it. An older InputPlumber parses a profile with layers
#         fine and silently ignores them (unknown fields are skipped).
#   0002  ours, for PR #757 (agreed with ShadowApex 2026-10-26): a mapping that holds a layer
#         down keeps its other outputs back until release, and sends them as a tap only if the
#         layer produced nothing meanwhile. Guide -> [layer, dbus ui_guide] then opens the OGUI
#         menu on a lone tap and stays silent after Guide+R1 (it used to send ui_guide on press,
#         so every chord also opened the menu). A profile load also releases what the active
#         layers produced first: OGUI loads its focus profile while Guide+South is still held, and
#         the lost ui_quick release made the DBus target drop the next press as a duplicate (quick
#         bar and OSK opened every other time). Upstream PR #771. Drop with 0001 once upstream
#         carries it.
#   0003  ours, build time only: main.rs declared the whole module tree again with its own `mod`
#         items instead of using lib.rs (which the `generate` schema tool needs), so cargo
#         compiled every module twice, once into the library and once into the daemon. The
#         daemon now `use`s the library. Same code, same log targets (both crates are named
#         inputplumber). Worth sending upstream; drop once a release does the same.
name: inputplumber
pkgbuild_local: PKGBUILD
patches: 0001-feat-Input-Layers-add-input-layers-to-map-button-com.patch 0002-feat-Input-Layers-a-held-activator-taps-its-other-outputs.patch 0003-fix-build-the-daemon-from-the-library-instead-of-compiling-twice.patch
pkgrel_suffix: 1
